    <summary>Desktop command center for ZMail, ZeroThink, OpenZero, CallChat, and local ZSEC Shield preview.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
ZERO ONE is a desktop command center for the TalkToAI ecosystem from QUANTUMENCRYPTION1 LTD / ResearchForumOnline.

## Features

- Four connected workspaces: ZMail, ZeroThink, OpenZero, and CallChat
- Isolated persistent sessions per workspace
- Stay signed in (ZeroThink + ZMail) with encrypted saved logins on Windows
- Optional local ZSEC Shield on-demand folder scan preview (Windows x64)

## Notes

- Installer is electron-builder NSIS (oneClick). Silent install uses `/S`.
- The bundled ZSEC Shield preview is **not** real-time antivirus protection.
- Remote workspaces require internet access and may need separate service accounts.

## Package source

- Homepage: https://talktoai.org/ZeroOne/
- Source: https://github.com/ResearchForumOnline/ZERO-ONE-Desktop
- License: Apache-2.0
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes><![CDATA[
0.6.3

- Stay signed in for ZeroThink and ZMail (longer-lived session cookies + restore on launch)
- Encrypted saved workspace logins via Windows DPAPI / Electron safeStorage
- Windows packaging and CI integrity fixes so version bumps do not break package builds

Release notes: https://github.com/ResearchForumOnline/ZERO-ONE-Desktop/releases/tag/v0.6.3
]]></releaseNotes>
